{"at":"2026-09-09T10:17","src":"cinema-extras.json, rooms.json and cinema-reviews.json, in docs/","fmt":{"dolby_atmos":{"es":"Dolby Atmos","en":"Object-based surround sound: speakers overhead as well as around you, so a sound can be placed and moved anywhere in the room rather than assigned to a fixed channel.","conf":"third_party","why":"Cinemex publishes no description. The definition is Dolby's own technology as described by Spanish Wikipedia. No channel count is claimed -- Cinemex publishes none, and a 7.1 figure would be a Cinepolis Macro XE claim."},"imax":{"es":"IMAX","en":"A very large, brighter screen with stadium seating, and a print remastered for the format -- up to 26% more picture on selected titles. Cinemex's most expensive ticket outside Platino.","conf":"operator_published","why":"CORRECTED. An earlier pass of this file said Cinemex publishes only marketing for IMAX and sourced the mechanism from Wikipedia. They publish a full description -- it is inside image `alt` attributes on their conoce-imax page, so a CMS reader that strips tags before searching finds nothing and concludes they say nothing. Spanish Wikipedia is kept as a second source for the screen geometry, which Cinemex does not give."},"infinity-vision":{"es":"Infinity Vision","en":"Not a Cinemex room type at all -- a Disney quality badge. Disney inspects a cinema's big screen and certifies it good enough to show Marvel films the way they were finished, and the badge rides on the film rather than the room. No new technology is involved; it is a promise about brightness, screen size and sound, aimed at IMAX.","conf":"third_party","why":"RESOLVED, and the reason Cinemex describes it nowhere is that it is not theirs to describe. Corroborated from this app's own data before either article was trusted: all 150 Infinity Vision showtimes here are ONE film, 'Avengers Endgame: Bonus', spread across six venues -- which is exactly the shape of a studio certification attached to a release, and not the shape of a room's permanent equipment. Disney established it on 16 April 2026 for Marvel titles beginning with the September 2026 Endgame re-release and Avengers: Doomsday in December."},"lang_es":{"es":"Español","en":"Spoken in Spanish -- a foreign film dubbed, or a Mexican film in its own language.","conf":"operator_published","why":"Cinemex has a separate 'dubbed / Doblada' key and does not use it anywhere in this app, so lang_es carries both cases."},"lang_sub":{"es":"Subtitulada","en":"Original soundtrack with Spanish subtitles.","conf":"operator_published","why":"Their own display name is 'Subtitulada'; the plain words are the standard meaning of that label in Mexican cinemas."},"platinum":{"es":"Platino","en":"Reclining seats with food and drink brought to your seat, and a drinks menu that now includes Topo Chico Hard Seltzer. The most expensive format, and no promo price ever applies to it.","conf":"operator_published","why":"Quoted from their own Platino landing page. The 'no promo applies' half is measured: every Platino session priced identically on a promo day and a plain day, and the Mania terms exclude the concept by name."},"premium":{"es":"Premium","en":"Eleven pesos more than the ordinary screen, at each of the four cinemas here where both can be compared. Cinemex never says what the extra buys.","conf":"measured","why":"The gap is exactly +$11 at all four app venues that price both Tradicional and Premium on the same plain day -- Pabellon Cuauhtemoc 94 to 105 both dubbed and subtitled, Galerias 90 to 101, Loreto 105 to 116. Four pairs is a small sample and it is the whole sample there is; the absolute price still varies a lot by venue. The word 'Premium' appears in Cinemex's CMS only as part of a cinema name or in a promo exclusion list, never with a description."},"traditional":{"es":"Tradicional","en":"The ordinary screen. The cheapest ticket at any cinema that has one, and the one the Wednesday-and-Thursday $39 promo is aimed at.","conf":"measured","why":"Tradicional is the lowest adult price at every venue measured, and it is one of the two concepts the Mania terms name."},"v3d":{"es":"3D","en":"A 3D screening; you wear the glasses.","conf":"label_translation","why":null}},"loyalty":{"name":"Cinemex Loop","tiers":[["Cinemex Loop One",3],["Cinemex Loop Red",5],["Cinemex Loop Gold",8],["Cinemex Loop Platino",10],["Arena XP Loop",5]],"point_value":null,"point_note":"Cinemex says points are spendable as a means of payment -- 'dichos puntos pueden usarse como medio de pago' -- and never states a points-to-pesos ratio anywhere in the 8.4 MB CMS or the benefits payload. Do not show a peso value for a Cinemex point.","packages":[{"name":"Arena XP Loop","tickets":1,"lo":49,"hi":49,"varies":false},{"name":"One","tickets":1,"lo":0,"hi":0,"varies":false},{"name":"Nivel Red - 5 boletos","tickets":5,"lo":249,"hi":959,"varies":true},{"name":"Red Tradicional","tickets":2,"lo":49,"hi":49,"varies":false},{"name":"Nivel Red - 10 boletos","tickets":10,"lo":429,"hi":969,"varies":true},{"name":"Red Platino","tickets":1,"lo":119,"hi":119,"varies":false}]},"promo":{"name":"Cinemexmania, September 2026","price":39,"days":"Monday to Thursday","window":"2026-09-07 to 2026-09-10","yes":["Tradicional","Premium"],"no":["Market","Platino","IMAX","4D","Dolby ATMOS"],"also_no":["premieres","funciones especiales","preventa","other promotions and discounts"]},"cineteca_price":{"general":70,"reduced":50,"reduced_for":["under 25","students","seniors"],"cheap_days":["Tuesday","Wednesday"],"cheap_price":50,"cheap_not":["Muestra","Foro","Talento emergente"],"max_tickets":8},"indie":[{"rating":4.5,"n":4778,"sampled":110,"themes":[["snack bar",42.7],["staff and service",41.8],["what is showing",40.9],["price",22.7]],"map":"Cine Tonala","name":"Cine Tonalá","url":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJzbWbjj3_0YURrt6mE5VJJLE&hl=es&gl=mx"},{"rating":4.7,"n":186,"sampled":87,"themes":[["seat comfort",10.3],["price",9.2],["what is showi